<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/10th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Valdejunquera</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">920</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Valdejunquera was fought on 26 July 920 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-rahman-iii">Abd al-Rahman III</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a>, on campaign against the Christian north, defeated the combined armies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ordono-ii-of-leon">Ordoño II of León</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sancho-garces-i-of-pamplona">Sancho Garcés I of Pamplona</a>, capturing several leading men. The victory showed the military superiority of the Umayyad state, which went on to sack <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pamplona">Pamplona</a> in 924.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-valdejunquera.jpg" alt="Battle of Valdejunquera" width="320" height="223" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Crates · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_Iberian_Peninsula_910-es.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
